cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EXEC_MAGICA: a collectible card-game benchmark for game-playing AI"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dmytro
    family-names: Kuzmenkov
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5981-2407"
abstract: >-
  EXEC_MAGICA is a turn-based collectible card game built as a research
  testbed for comparing decision-making algorithms under hidden information
  and stochasticity. It provides a reproducible pipeline for evaluating
  game-playing AI agents and a playable client for human-vs-AI and
  AI-vs-AI matches.
keywords:
  - game-playing AI
  - Monte-Carlo Tree Search
  - collectible card game
  - imperfect information
  - decision-making under uncertainty
license: MIT
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-06-27
url: "https://github.com/kuzmenkoff/exec_magica"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kuzmenkoff/exec_magica"

